    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-5">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-teal-500"></span>
            1. Dense-Phase CO2 Solubility &amp; Retrograde Thermodynamic Saturation
          </h3>
          <p>
            Supercritical CO2 possesses liquid-like density and gas-like diffusivity. In high-viscosity hydrocolloid purees (pectin, cellulose, proteins), CO2 gas dissolution follows Henry's law:
          </p>
          <div class="my-2.5 p-2.5 bg-slate-900 text-teal-300 font-mono text-xs rounded-xl text-center overflow-x-auto">
            C_CO2 = k_H(T) · P_CO2 · exp[(v_m · (P - P_sat)) / (R · T)]
          </div>
          <p>
            At operating pressures between 80 and 160 bar and 35°C, CO2 dissolves rapidly into the aqueous phase (3.0–5.5 wt%), reducing puree apparent viscosity by 35% through plasticization of biopolymer chains.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-5">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-teal-500"></span>
            2. Classical Nucleation &amp; Slit-Die Controlled Pressure Drop
          </h3>
          <p>
            As the saturated puree flows through the high-pressure slit-die nozzle, the local pressure drops at rates exceeding <strong>ΔP/Δt &gt; 400 bar/s</strong>. The thermodynamic supersaturation ratio S triggers homogenous bubble nucleation:
          </p>
          <div class="my-2.5 p-2.5 bg-slate-900 text-teal-300 font-mono text-xs rounded-xl text-center overflow-x-auto">
            J_nuc = N_0 · exp[-16 π γ³ / (3 k_B T (ΔP)²)]
          </div>
          <p>
            Over 10⁶ micro-bubbles nucleate per cubic centimeter, expanding into a uniform micro-cellular honeycomb with cell diameters between 15 and 45 µm and an open-cell fraction exceeding 92%.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-5">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-teal-500"></span>
            3. Non-Destructive In-Line Ultrasonic Acoustic Porosimetry (DIP)
          </h3>
          <p>
            Continuous real-time monitoring of foam porosity and pore size distribution is achieved via non-contact ultrasonic transducers operating at 400 kHz. Biot's acoustic propagation in porous media dictates wave attenuation:
          </p>
          <div class="my-2.5 p-2.5 bg-slate-900 text-teal-300 font-mono text-xs rounded-xl text-center overflow-x-auto">
            α(f) = (2 π f / c_0) · [ (1 - ε) / 2 ] · [ η / (ρ_foam · a_pore²) ]^(1/2)
          </div>
          <p>
            The acoustic attenuation coefficient α directly tracks structural foam density and wall thickness without interrupting product conveyor movement, alerting operators to bubble collapse in real time.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-5">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-teal-500"></span>
            4. Sublimation &amp; Convective Desorption at Ambient Temperatures
          </h3>
          <p>
            Because the open-cell foam expands the effective specific evaporation surface area by over <strong>40-fold</strong>, moisture diffusion distance across thin cell walls (δ_wall &lt; 4 µm) is negligible. Mass flux is described by:
          </p>
          <div class="my-2.5 p-2.5 bg-slate-900 text-teal-300 font-mono text-xs rounded-xl text-center overflow-x-auto">
            J_water = h_m · A_foam · [ a_w · P_sat(T) - P_air_vapor ]
          </div>
          <p>
            Drying to shelf-stable water activity (a_w &lt; 0.25) finishes in under 8–10 minutes at 35°C, preserving &gt;97.5% vitamin C and &gt;92% live probiotic bacterial counts.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
